    47	def cylindrical_pose_features(
    48	    md: Dict[str, object], eps: float = 1e-6
    49	) -> Dict[str, object]:
    50	    """
    51	    Replace absolute pose vectors with yaw-invariant cylindrical features.
    52	
    53	    Each pose ``(x, y, z)`` becomes ``(r, z, dphi)`` where ``r = sqrt(x^2 + y^2)``
    54	    and ``dphi`` is the azimuth measured *relative* to a scene-intrinsic reference
    55	    azimuth. Because every azimuth in a rigidly yaw-rotated scene shifts by the
    56	    same amount, the relative ``dphi`` (and ``r``, ``z``) are invariant under any
    57	    yaw rotation, making these features an exact invariant of the C-infinity yaw
    58	    group.
    59	
    60	    The reference azimuth is the target source's azimuth. If the source lies on
    61	    the vertical axis (``r_s < eps``, azimuth undefined) the reference falls back
    62	    to the azimuth of the largest-``r`` pose among ``{source, context poses}`` --
    63	    still a scene-intrinsic quantity, so invariance is preserved in the fallback.
    64	    If *every* pose is degenerate (largest ``r`` also ``< eps``) every ``dphi``
    65	    is exactly ``0``.
    66	
    67	    Only ``'source'`` and ``'context_poses'`` are transformed; ``'*_vit'`` poses,
    68	    ``'depth'`` and all other keys pass through untouched (same objects). The
    69	    input dict is not mutated: a shallow copy is returned with fresh tensors for
    70	    the replaced keys, preserving each pose tensor's dtype and device.
    71	
    72	    Parameters
    73	    ----------
    74	    md : Dict[str, object]
    75	        One per-sample metadata dict. ``'source'`` (shape ``[3]``) and, optionally,
    76	        ``'context_poses'`` (shape ``[N, 3]``) are read; the last dimension is
    77	        ordered ``(x, y, z)``.
    78	    eps : float, optional
    79	        Radius below which a pose azimuth is treated as undefined (default 1e-6).
    80	
    81	    Returns
    82	    -------
    83	    Dict[str, object]
