   165	) -> Dict[str, object]:
   166	    """
   167	    Apply a physically-consistent yaw rotation to a single sample's metadata.
   168	
   169	    The equirectangular depth map is rolled horizontally by the integer number of
   170	    columns closest to ``alpha_rad`` and its stored per-pixel 3D vectors are rotated
   171	    about z. All pose vectors are rotated about z by the same effective angle.
   172	    ``context_audio``, ``scene`` and any other field pass through unchanged. The
   173	    rotation is exact (no interpolation) because the column shift is quantised and
   174	    the rotation matrix uses the matching effective angle.
   175	
   176	    Parameters
   177	    ----------
   178	    md : Dict[str, object]
   179	        One per-sample metadata dict as produced by the AR/HAA metadata module.
   180	        Expected tensor fields: ``depth`` of shape ``[3, H, W]`` and pose fields
   181	        (``source``, ``source_vit``, ``context_poses``, ``context_poses_vit``)
   182	        whose last dimension is 3.
   183	    alpha_rad : float
   184	        Requested yaw rotation angle in radians.
   185	    img_w : int
   186	        Panorama width in pixels (number of azimuth columns), e.g. 512.
   187	    pose_keys : Tuple[str, ...], optional
   188	        Which pose fields to rotate. Defaults to rotating all of ``POSE_KEYS``.
   189	        Restricting it (e.g. to the ``*_vit`` keys only) leaves the unlisted pose
   190	        fields bit-identical; ``depth`` handling is unaffected.
   191	
   192	    Returns
   193	    -------
   194	    Dict[str, object]
   195	        A shallow-copied metadata dict with ``depth`` and the selected pose fields
   196	        replaced by their rotated versions. The original dict is not mutated.
   197	    """
   198	    dj = int(round(alpha_rad * img_w / (2.0 * math.pi))) % img_w
   199	    alpha_eff = dj * 2.0 * math.pi / img_w
   200	    rot = azimuth_rotation_matrix(alpha_eff)
