+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
+# Trained-as protocol guard
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
+# A checkpoint trained under 'fa_invariant' but evaluated with vanilla
+# conditioning (or the reverse) produces plausible-looking numbers that are
+# catastrophically wrong in BOTH directions, so the evaluation protocol must
+# never come from a CLI default. It does not have to: the training method is
+# recoverable from the checkpoint, and evaluation therefore INHERITS it and
+# refuses a contradicting explicit request unless deliberately overridden.
