   204	
   205	### Baselines
   206	We provide a unified evaluation script that supports multiple baseline methods. The baselines serve as comparison points for learned generative models by using simple heuristics based on spatial proximity or random selection.
   207	
   208	The following baseline methods are supported:
   209	- RdnAcross: Randomly samples a RIR from the entire dataset. This baseline ignores all spatial information and serves as a lower bound on performance.
   210	- RdnSame: Randomly samples a RIR from the same room/scene as the target. This baseline uses room identity but ignores the specific source-receiver positions.
   211	- KNN: K-Nearest Neighbor approach that selects the reference RIR whose source position is closest to the target source position. This baseline uses explicit spatial reasoning with `--num-shot` reference examples.
   212	- LinearInterp: Linear interpolation of multiple reference RIRs weighted by inverse distance to the target source position. Uses `--num-shot` reference examples and performs weighted interpolation in the waveform domain.
   213	
   214	The `eval_baselines.py` script handles both AR and HAA datasets:
   215	
   216	```bash
   217	# AR (KNN 8-shot unseen evaluation)
   218	python -m baselines.eval_baselines \
   219	--dataset AR \
   220	--baseline KNN \
   221	--num-shot 8 \
   222	--split unseen \
   223	--data-path /path/to/AR/dataset \
   224	--seen-json data/AR/seen_eval.json \
   225	--ckpt-AGREE weights/AGREE/AGREE_fullAR.pt \
   226	--out-dir baselines_results
   227	
   228	# HAA (RdnAcross test evaluation)
   229	python -m baselines.eval_baselines \
   230	--dataset HAA \
   231	--baseline RdnAcross \
   232	--split-file data/HAA/test_base.json \
   233	--data-path /path/to/HAA_dataset \
   234	--ckpt-AGREE weights/AGREE/AGREE_fullHAA.pt \
   235	--out-dir baselines_results/
   236	```
   237	
   238	
   239	### VAE 
   240	To eval the VAE:
   241	
   242	```bash
   243	python eval_VAE.py \
   244	--model-config /path/to/model/config \
   245	--dataset-config /path/to/eval/dataset/config \
   246	--eval-name eval_VAE \
   247	--ckpt-path /path/to/VAE/ckpt
   248	```
   249	**Note**: You need to give the `.ckpt` file in that case, not the `.safetensors` file.
